  "body": "Found in the review read of PR #3668 (the catalog case `3d/rough-finish`, #2866). Read from the posted program; no machine run. Refs #2392.\n\n**What the program does:** between two levels the tool makes a rapid straight down to the Z of the floor that it cut in the level before, with no margin. Examples: line 63 `G00 X-23.98 Y-24.03 Z20.`, line 1625 `G00 ... Z10.`. The lowest Z on a rapid line of the program is Z10.\n\n**Risk:** a rapid that ends in contact with a floor that was cut a moment ago. A small error of the tool length, or chips on the floor, makes it a rapid into material. The usual practice is to stop the rapid a feed distance above the floor and to feed the rest.\n\n**Expected:** the rapid stops at the feed height above the last cut floor (the feed height of the operation), and the rest is a feed move.\n\n**Done when:** a test on this case finds no rapid whose end is nearer to cut or uncut material than the feed height. The catalog program is then made again.\n",
